+# Agent Note: Provider-neutral model cost accounting
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-15-provider-neutral-model-cost-accounting.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Token usage alone cannot distinguish provider-reported spend, tariff estimates, and virtual subscription reference values. Repricing historical calls from a current catalog changes history, while a separate cost event can commit before or after its Assistant settlement and lose atomic attribution on a crash.
+
+## Decision
+
+`dsh-llm` keeps monetary accounting separate from `TokenUsage`. A model adapter may emit one `accounting` chunk containing non-empty `ModelCallAccounting.costs`; each cost names its `reported`, `estimated`, or `virtual` kind, uppercase currency identifier, non-negative safe-integer nanos, source, optional tariff version, and optional same-currency component nanos.
+
+The stream invariant permits at most one accounting chunk before `finish`. The Agent Loop copies the validated value onto the same `assistant/message` or `assistant/attempt` that stores the exact stream, so accounting and attempt settlement commit atomically. Calls without accounting remain valid and do not acquire a zero value.
+
+The token-meter package derives complete normal-Turn costs through the durable attempt, retry, step, and Turn lifecycle. Any settled attempt without valid accounting makes that Turn's cost unavailable. The `modelCost` Session projection adds only complete Turn summaries, groups totals by currency and kind without conversion, and publishes accounted versus unaccounted model-Turn coverage so consumers present accumulated values as known subtotals when coverage is incomplete.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Adding money to `TokenUsage` was rejected because token measurement and monetary provenance have different semantics and availability. A separate Session event was rejected because the public append API cannot atomically bind it to the Assistant settlement. Repricing from the latest model catalog was rejected because it rewrites historical meaning after tariff changes. Binary floating-point amounts and implicit currency conversion were rejected because cumulative results would not be exact or reproducible.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Provider adapters own cost classification and source provenance; this change supplies no provider tariff or monetary value by itself. Safe-integer nanos bound one stored amount and every aggregate to `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`. Normal-Turn totals include failed and retried attempts only when every settlement carries accounting. Session-title, compaction, and child-Session calls remain outside `modelCost`.
+
+The optional accounting fields extend Assistant settlements and embedded streams without changing model-visible history. The pinned predecessor snapshots raw chunks as lossless JSON and its assembler ignores an unknown raw chunk, so it can open these settlements while omitting monetary accounting; current-generation verification additionally enforces accounting order and top-level/embedded equality.
+
+## Verification
+
+The LLM suites validate exact fields, ordering, duplicate rejection, safe nanos, bounded component sums, assembler copies, compact-stream reconstruction, and invariant failures. Current-generation persistence tests reject duplicate, late, missing, or contradictory embedded accounting. Agent Loop tests prove top-level and embedded accounting settle together for messages and attempts. Token-meter tests cover retries, mixed kinds, currencies, unsafe sums, incomplete Turns, projection replay, and coverage of unaccounted model Turns.
