+## Model-call monetary accounting
+
+Accounting remains separate from token usage. Each cost is an additive amount in safe integer nanos, classified as provider-reported, tariff-estimated, or a virtual subscription reference value. Currency conversion is outside this contract; optional component nanos inherit the cost's currency, sum to no more than the total so an unclassified remainder is allowed, and retain source and tariff provenance with the amount.
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** Whether a monetary value was provider-reported, tariff-estimated, or a subscription reference equivalent. */
+type ModelCostKind = 'reported' | 'estimated' | 'virtual'
+```
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** One exact non-negative amount in billionths of its named currency unit. */
+interface MonetaryAmount {
+  readonly currency: string
+  readonly nanos: number
+}
+```
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** Optional additive components whose currency is inherited from the owning cost amount. */
+interface ModelCostBreakdown {
+  readonly inputNanos?: number
+  readonly outputNanos?: number
+  readonly cacheReadNanos?: number
+  readonly cacheWriteNanos?: number
+}
+```
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** One independently additive monetary value attributed to a model call. */
+interface ModelCallCost {
+  readonly kind: ModelCostKind
+  readonly amount: MonetaryAmount
+  readonly source: string
+  readonly tariffVersion?: string
+  readonly breakdown?: ModelCostBreakdown
+}
+```
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/** Provider-neutral monetary accounting emitted for one model call. */
+interface ModelCallAccounting {
+  /** Non-empty additive values; duplicate kind/currency pairs are forbidden within one call. */
+  readonly costs: readonly ModelCallCost[]
+}
+```
+
+`validateModelCallAccounting()` rejects unknown fields, empty costs, duplicate kind/currency pairs, malformed provenance, non-uppercase currency identifiers, and negative or unsafe nanos. The LLM stream invariant accepts at most one accounting chunk before finish. The exact compact stream retains that chunk, while the agent loop copies the same accounting top-level onto `assistant/message` or `assistant/attempt` in the settlement transaction.
